From d02237695a7722e2f1dd792484068e3d09a8ff32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:04:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] dsv41: TF_DS_IDX_FUSED (off by default): the candidate
 pool's blockMax -> topk_indices -> poolPick in one launch

TF_DS_IDX_FUSED gates the source chains of the indexer's candidate pool behind a switch that
parses unset/""/0/1 (anything else refuses to start), off by default: the decode candidate-source
layer (round.zig) and the prompt chunk's pooled source layer (prompt.zig). One block per row:
the block maxima (the amax NaN-wins rule with the newest block pinned to +inf), the top-k over
them (tf_ds_topk_select_row, the same selection tf_ds_topk_indices_kernel launches, extracted
verbatim and shared) and the pool's mask u8 / block list (the pool_pick rule), in one launch.
The mask application (applyPool) and the candFast case stay unfused: each is already one launch,
so there is nothing to fold. Past 8192 maxima blocks (or a bad switch, or a cap on TF_DS_T13)
the unfused launches run; the selection's vis stays the every_vis constant, as at both call sites.
UNVERIFIED-BUILD on this machine (no nvcc): gated on the exact suite on a Spark like 0193/0194.
